{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556112-new-wolf-gift-gift-of-the-chase","id":1556112,"title":"[New Wolf Gift] Gift of The Chase","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-02T21:48:52-08:00","id":1556112,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [New Wolf Gift] Gift of The Chase","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a Wolf Gift I made inspired by the homebrew <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1370046-feedback-requested-gift-of-the-wyrd\">Gift of the Wyrd</a>. It was made using some of the advice given by Chris Allen, following his advice in both the guide and advice on his patreon/articles and I think I did a fair job on it. I understand some of these facets could perhaps exist in other existing shadow gifts, but these gifts are meant to be more direct aids in chasing prey while allowing for some intermingling of different gamelines and I don't believe there is any direct overlap that I can remember. Advice or opinions would be appreciated, especially about the specific numbers and essence costs of the various gifts.</span></span><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gift of the Chase</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Gift of the Chase is a welcome gift to many wolves, as it encapsulates and aids in a great number of aspects of the hunt. However, unlocking these facets can only be done when at the completion of a Sacred Hunt, and only one may be purchased at a time. The Ithauer are unsure of why this would be, but Cahalith tell stories of the trials of the First Pack, and the importance of their first chase alongside Urfarah.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Eyes of the Oath Keeper (Cunning)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It\u2019s important to know when your prey has promises or loose ends that could complicate the chase.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Essence</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Wits + Politics + Cunning</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The uratha can use this facet on any prey whom they have studied for one turn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Roll Results</i></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Facet fails, and the werewolf gains the Ban Condition; she must agree to any favor or deal offered to her until the end of the scene.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Facet fails to inform you of the prey\u2019s dealings..</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Uratha becomes aware if the prey is part of a supernatural or mundane dealing or oath. Only serious mundane deals will be made clear to the Uratha, specifically if they somehow pertain to her or the hunt. This is best used to inform her of if her prey is under compulsion of a spirit or other threat of the People, but can just as easily inform her if her prey is under the effects of a pledge, sealing (Changeling), or even, the domination of supernatural (Vampire) compelling them to agree to an oath. While this facet does not reveal normally reveal intimate details of a binding, it does immediately reveal if the obligation is supernaturally enforced or not.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The hunter gains more immediate details of the deal itself, such as if the prey is trading weapons dangerous to the Uratha, or if there is spiritual compulsion involved. While this facet will not reveal explicitly who is on the other side of a dealing, it can often be a key component in identifying them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Surrender The Prey (Glory)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Allies of prey are often stubborn to give up their friends, but hands-off persuasion can be just as useful as tooth and claw.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Scene</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once this Facet is activated, the Uratha gains the Badass Motherfucker advantage as if she was in Dalu. If used in any other form than Hishu or Urhan, the prey\u2019s roll to resist suffers a penalty equal to the Uratha\u2019s Glory renown. If this would trigger a Clash of Wills while in Dalu, Urshul, or Gauru, the Uratha\u2019s Clash of Wills is made as an advanced action.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Rebuke The Shackles (Honor)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Deals often made during the frenzy of a chase are rarely thought through, it is for these reasons that even Father Wolf knew many were made to be broken.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 or 3 Essence</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Manipulation + Subterfuge + Honor</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This facet is used primarily when confronted with proof of a deal or promise made, often in pursuit of aiding a hunt. Alternatively, for 3 Essence, it may be used when confronted with a supernatural deal or promise made in an attempt to free themselves of such shackles.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Roll Results</i></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The facet fails and any mundane proof of the deal becomes more damning, nearly impossible to try and deny. Targeted supernatural deals cause the Uratha to gain the Ban condition; she must adhere to the spirit of the deal as well as the letter to the best of her ability.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Facet fails with no effect.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Mundane proof of any deal made between the Uratha and associated parties becomes unreliable. Signatures are missing in core parts of the paperwork or the paperwork alludes to a different kind of deal than initially thought, perhaps even memories of the arrangement become difficult to recall for any but the Uratha. Supernatural oaths or deals are broken, freeing the Uratha from precarious agreement. Any provoked Clash of Wills checks made by the Uratha add her Honor renown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Mundane dealings become impossible to prove. Evidence goes missing, files are corrupted, and memories suddenly gain large gaps regarding the arrangement. Provoked Clash of Wills checks gain the rote action property.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Surefooted Predator (Purity)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The chase is part of the hunt, however, it is the final hurdle before the kill. Any Uratha knows that to overcome this hurdle, they can\u2019t waste time doubting their footing.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Permanent</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Uratha gains a bonus to their speed equal to their Purity Renown. While running, an Uratha may lower their speed by up to their Purity renown to ignore the same number in dice penalties to a foot chase.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sniff The Hidden Path (Wisdom)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It doesn\u2019t matter where the prey runs to try and escape you. Even if it\u2019s somewhere beyond the hisil, the nose knows.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None or 3 essence</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Uratha gains the ability to see entrances to other realms besides the shadow, such as trods or avernian gates. She gains a bonus equal to her Wisdom renown to dice pools to track her prey through such entrances or resist the supernatural effects of such realms. She may also spend a point of essence to temporarily reopen any shut portals that have not been closed for longer than 24 hours. Though, she must be careful to make her way back in time, lest she become trapped in one of these realms as the portal only remains open for a number of hours equal to twice her Wisdom renown.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28400-sigvardthediablerist","name":"SigvardTheDiablerist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28400_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}